# Separate correction review

The original 573-file candidate and 141-file independent negative review remain immutable. Their manifest SHA-256 values are respectively `7f975ae3f7a0827f5b9ade231bd121c5b4028f17d88758455fd680962ff0f878` and `76c89a780e5c8e2a7774d925073b500a1e8a5f5c164c86a6e4e71b809717db31`.

This is preparation only. No candidate imports, browser, host, behavioral tests or original execution begin before the correction author's exact freeze is supplied and authenticated.

Fresh actual browser cases will use owned synthetic LF, CRLF, bare-CR and mixed-ending files with preceding astral characters, repeated matches and both literal and regex searches. Native textarea selections will be compared with the exact normalized displayed string. Pending read/options/Save publications and accepted clean Close will exercise existing generation/draft boundaries. Native dirty-close cancellation, if the browser tool supports the confirmation dialog, is a separate observed control; inability to operate that dialog will be retained as incomplete evidence.

The proposed owned HTTP bridge exposes only bounded list/read/search/save and an explicit `gitStatus` stub. It does not run the shared Studio host or an original workbench. A token remains memory-only, request observations are persisted incrementally, and an explicit authenticated loopback shutdown replaces the previous closed-stdin driver. The earlier forced-cleanup failure is not rewritten or presented as a successful graceful shutdown.

Any author model adaptations are historical author evidence, not additional independently selected browser checks. The prior original cohort's six equal and two unequal groups remain separate; no native original execution is needed solely for source-offset-to-DOM correction.
